  "statement": "Find and classify all stationary points of $f(x)=x^{4}-4x^{3}+4x^{2}$.",
  "solution": "$f'(x)=4x^{3}-12x^{2}+8x=4x(x^{2}-3x+2)=4x(x-1)(x-2)$, so stationary points at $x=0,1,2$. $f''(x)=12x^{2}-24x+8$. At $x=0$: $f''(0)=8>0$ so a minimum, $f(0)=0$. At $x=1$: $f''(1)=-4<0$ so a maximum, $f(1)=1$. At $x=2$: $f''(2)=8>0$ so a minimum, $f(2)=0$.",
  "hints": [
    "Factorise $f'(x)$ completely.",
    "Use the second derivative to classify each critical point."
  ],
